(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-sewing-operation :finalize-sewing-execution-decision :finalize-embroidery-operation :finalize-embroidery-execution-decision :declare-workshop-safety-cleared :declare-safety-clearance :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "2799007319-cloud-itonami-isco-7319-handicraft-workers-nec-coverage" "2799007317-cloud-itonami-isco-7317-handicraft-workers-wood-basketry-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "finalize the sewing operation" "finalize the sewing execution decision" "finalize the embroidery operation" "finalize the embroidery execution decision" "proceed with the sewing execution" "proceed with the embroidery execution" "authorize the sewing execution" "authorize the embroidery execution" "declare the workshop safety cleared" "declare workshop safety cleared" "declare the item safety-cleared" "declare the item safety cleared" "declare safety-cleared" "declare quality-cleared" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override shop safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799007533), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}"), (:actor/domain :manufacturing/sewing-embroidery-workshop-scheduling-logistics-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :worker-verified :workshop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "7533"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007533: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7533 Sewing, Embroidery and Related Workers workshop scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7533\n-- Sewing, Embroidery and Related Workers** only, Wave3\n(production/trades) of the rollout.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7533\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7533\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Sewing, Embroidery and Related\nWorkers\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the\nentry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no\nrepository existed at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7533` (`gh\napi` 404 confirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion\nregistry edit promote the `7533` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nISCO-08 7533 workers operate sewing and embroidery machines, so this\nvertical carries a concrete, machine-specific workshop hazard profile\n-- needle-puncture injury and moving-machine-part injury -- distinct\nfrom a residual/generic craft category. The controlling constraint for\nthis vertical is that the closed op allowlist must NEVER include any\nop that directly finalizes a sewing/embroidery-execution decision\n(e.g. deciding a sewing or embroidery job is finished) or a\nworkshop-safety-clearance decision (e.g. declaring a workshop or item\nsafety-cleared), nor override a shop safety officer's judgment --\nthose decisions must always be a hard permanent block, never\nauto-commit-eligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to WORKSHOP\nSCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs sewing or\nembroidery work and never makes a safety-clearance decision itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored closely for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7319`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7319)\n(Handicraft Workers Not Elsewhere Classified: `store`/`advisor`/\n`governor`/`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set,\nalready landed with a closely-related workshop-scheduling/logistics\nsafety pattern) -- cloned and read in full in this session (the more\ndirectly on-topic sibling, `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7531`\n\"Tailors, Dressmakers, Furriers and Hatters\", did not yet exist at\nscaffold time: `gh api` returned 404, so the fallback reference named\nin the task, 7319, was used per the task's own fallback instruction).\nIts `deps.edn` `langgraph` git-sha pin was reused verbatim for this\nrepo. The domain entity naming was deliberately changed from 7319's\ngeneric `artisan`/`workshop` to this repo's own `worker`/`workshop`\n(matching this task's own CRITICAL-invariant wording, \"worker/workshop\nrecord must be independently verified/registered before any action\"),\nand the hazard vocabulary was deliberately changed from 7319's generic\n`hand-tool-hazard`/`material-handling-hazard` to this repo's own\nmachine-specific `needle-puncture-hazard`/`machine-part-hazard`,\nmatching this occupation's concrete sewing/embroidery-machine hazard\nprofile rather than reusing a residual-category's deliberately generic\none.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7533` as an OSS workshop\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for sewing/embroidery\nworkshops, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as every\nprior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Sewing Coordination\nAdvisor ⊣ SewCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with\nan independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **workshop scheduling/logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct sewing/embroidery-execution or\nsafety-clearance authority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise,\nsimulate exercising, or propose exercising a sewing/embroidery-\nexecution decision (e.g. deciding a sewing or embroidery job is\nfinished), a workshop-safety-clearance decision (e.g. declaring a\nworkshop or item safety-cleared), or any override of a shop safety\nofficer's judgment. These are not merely gated behind escalation --\nthey are structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- job/commission/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a needle-puncture-hazard/\n  machine-part-hazard/equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates,\n  NEVER auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- thread/fabric-materials procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nsewing/embroidery-execution decision, a workshop-safety-clearance\ndecision, or a shop-safety-officer-judgment override. These are\n**structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely**, not merely\ngated behind escalation -- an op such as `:finalize-sewing-operation`\ncannot even be proposed by the reference mock advisor (its\n`infer`/`rationale-for` functions only ever emit one of the four\nallowlist ops), and if any code path (a forged proposal, a future LLM\nadvisor, a misbehaving fork) ever produced such an op, the governor's\nclosed-allowlist HARD check (`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally\nand permanently. A second, independent HARD check\n(`:scope-excluded-action`) names eight concretely-forbidden ops\n(`sewcoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`: `:finalize-sewing-operation`,\n`:finalize-sewing-execution-decision`, `:finalize-embroidery-operation`,\n`:finalize-embroidery-execution-decision`,\n`:declare-workshop-safety-cleared`, `:declare-safety-clearance`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`sewcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-sewing-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-embroidery-execution-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-workshop-safety-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nplus a full-graph-run regression\n(`sewcoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`,\n`.../holds-a-workshop-safety-clearance-op-even-at-high-confidence`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Worker unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered crew-member record (`:no-worker`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the worker is.\n2. **Workshop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered workshop (`:no-workshop`). Together with\n   check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a\n   worker/workshop record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the eight\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for finalizing a sewing or\n   embroidery operation, declaring a workshop safety-clearance, or\n   overriding a shop safety officer's judgment, is a second HARD,\n   PERMANENT block (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated\n   unconditionally on content -- defense-in-depth on top of the\n   allowlist check: even if a future change somehow widened the\n   allowlist, content-based rejection still independently blocks\n   sewing/embroidery-execution/safety-clearance-override language\n   wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a needle-puncture-\n  hazard/machine-part-hazard/equipment-condition observation -- it\n  never resolves the concern itself, and the robot's role ends at\n  \"here is the hazard data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing\n  about shop safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  thread/fabric-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  sewing/embroidery-execution/safety-clearance/safety-officer-override\n  attempt, which is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft\n  escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"sewing\", \"embroidery\", \"safety\") can accidentally match inside the\nmock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk\nCLAUDE.md's worked example warns about for this task.\n`sewcoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as\nfinalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"finalize the sewing operation\",\n\"declare the workshop safety cleared\", \"override the shop safety\nofficer's judgment\" -- matching the task's own worked example phrasing\nverbatim), never bare nouns, and\n`sewcoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for worker ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\nsewing/embroidery task ...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer\nreview\") WITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action\nphrases, so the regression test is a genuine stress test of the\nbare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on\nfirst run in this session -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard\nitself was never tripped during development.\n`sewcoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nand `.../holds-a-workshop-safety-clearance-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercise the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7533\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7533` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7533`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 24 tests, 52 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- clj-kondo (`clojure -M:lint`) clean: 0 errors, 0 warnings (two\n  findings caught and fixed during development: an unused `:as\n  request` destructure binding, and a JVM-only bare `read-string` call\n  replaced with the portable `clojure.edn/read-string` to keep the\n  `.cljc` source truly cljs-first/portable per CLAUDE.md's mandatory\n  runtime-portability rule -- the reference repo's own `:lint` alias\n  turned out not to be wired into its `deps.edn` at all, so this\n  particular defect had never actually been caught upstream).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-sewing-execution` or\n  `:approve-safety-clearance` that is merely gated behind an\n  always-escalate list (the shape `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for\n  `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`): rejected outright per the task's\n  explicit domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op still means\n  the *capability* to finalize a sewing/embroidery-execution or\n  safety-clearance decision exists in the code path and is merely\n  deferred to a human gate. For a decision this severe (needle-\n  puncture injury, moving-machine-part injury, workshop-safety\n  clearance), the capability itself must not exist. The only op\n  related to shop-safety escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which\n  surfaces the need for human/shop-safety-officer attention and never\n  itself decides, authorizes, or defers a sewing/embroidery-execution\n  or safety-clearance decision for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold thread/fabric-\n  materials order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft\n  escalate gate, not a hard block; only the sewing/embroidery-\n  execution/safety-clearance/safety-officer-override class is a hard,\n  unconditional block.\n- Reusing 7319's generic `artisan` entity name and generic\n  `hand-tool-hazard`/`material-handling-hazard` vocabulary verbatim:\n  rejected -- ISCO-08 7533 is a concrete sewing/embroidery-machine\n  occupation with a well-defined, non-residual hazard profile\n  (needle-puncture injury, moving-machine-part injury) and this task's\n  own CRITICAL invariant text names the entity \"worker\" explicitly, so\n  this repo's own domain vocabulary (`worker`, `needle-puncture-\n  hazard`, `machine-part-hazard`) was used instead of the 7319\n  reference's deliberately generic residual-category terms.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"sewing\" \"embroidery\"\n  \"safety\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses\n  sewing/embroidery/safety-officer concepts to do its\n  scheduling/logging job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking\n  the actor's own legitimate proposals (regression-tested directly\n  against rationale text that deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Merging `worker` and `workshop` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered worker AND independently-registered\n  workshop) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/workshop\n  record must be independently verified/registered before any action\"\n  and the established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors\n  with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- job/commission/progress data logging\n   only. Requires an independently registered worker AND workshop\n   (`:no-worker`/`:no-workshop`). Not a sewing/embroidery-execution or\n   workshop-safety-clearance decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry a sewing/embroidery-execution decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content\n   check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about\n   a specific sewing or embroidery job -- it is a calendar/logistics\n   action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a needle-puncture-hazard/\n   machine-part-hazard/equipment-condition concern to a human/shop\n   safety officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every\n   confidence level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY\n   channel through which a safety observation may be surfaced, and it\n   explicitly never resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself --\n   the shop safety officer reviews and acts entirely on their own\n   authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- thread/fabric-materials\n   procurement proposal only (item, cost). Not a sewing/embroidery-\n   execution or workshop-safety-clearance decision of any kind -- it\n   is a purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na sewing/embroidery-execution decision (e.g. deciding a sewing or\nembroidery job is finished), a workshop-safety-clearance decision\n(e.g. declaring a workshop or item safety-cleared), or a\nshop-safety-officer-judgment override -- these categories are\nstructurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op\nallowlist itself (`sewcoord.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) eight\nconcretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit\nlevel (`sewcoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`sewcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-sewing-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-embroidery-execution-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-workshop-safety-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`sewcoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to finalize a sewing operation, declare a workshop\nsafety-cleared, or override a shop safety officer's judgment even via\nan otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`sewcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-declare-workshop-safety-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`).\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}"), (:test/counts "{:total 24, :assertions 52, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Sewing and Embroidery Workshop Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :worker-verification :workshop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7533"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7533"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7533)), (:test/simulator :sewcoord.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7533 — Sewing, Embroidery and Related Workers Workshop Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7533)))
